Generated by the improve-animations skill. Execute in the order below unless dependencies say otherwise. Each executor: read the plan fully, honor STOP conditions, and update your row when done.

## Execution order & status

| Plan | Title | Severity | Category | Status |
|------|-------|----------|----------|--------|
| 001 | Gate button motion for reduced motion and touch | HIGH | Accessibility | DONE |
| 002 | Fix exiting slide easing | MEDIUM | Easing | DONE |
| 003 | Soften nav celebration bounce | MEDIUM | Physicality / Cohesion | DONE |
| 004 | Introduce motion tokens | LOW | Cohesion / Tokens | DONE |

## Dependency notes

- 001 is independent and first priority (accessibility).
- 002 and 003 touch `src/chinese-java/swipe.html` but different lines; either order is fine.
- 004 is low-risk and independent, but doing it after 001-003 avoids conflicting edits in the same CSS file.

## Findings considered and rejected

- CSS button system uses transform/opacity transitions, so no `transition: all` or layout-property animation findings.
- No `scale(0)` instances were found in the motion code.
- GSAP motion is already gated by `k = 0` for reduced motion; only CSS transitions lack a media query, captured in 001.
